WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:03.110
Dr. Reynard had lost everything.

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:09.440
His job, the respect of his peers, and if
everyone else was right, perhaps even his

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.440
mind.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.889
It was eleven PM when he staggered to the
edge of Okanagan Lake, in British Columbia,

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:17.980
eyes and judgment clouded with booze.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:23.380
This lake could have been what made his career
as a researcher for the SCP Foundation, but

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:28.760
now that bright future was slipping through
his fingers like the dry silt beneath his

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:29.760
feet.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:35.010
He looked hatefully across the endless, dark
surface of the water and loudly cursed.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.440
Stupid, empty place.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.810
Just hours ago, he’d been stripped of his
ranks and released from his position at the

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:46.390
Foundation, for wasting the organization’s
time and resources on frivolous personal projects.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.540
Frivolous, he thought.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.280
What a terrible joke.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.320
Just because the higher-ups refused to acknowledge
what was going on out here didn’t mean it

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.320
wasn’t there.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.320
Dr. Reynard sighed and took another long swig
from his scotch bottle.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:01.550
Moonlight shimmered off the water’s surface...Wait,
was that moonlight, or was something lurking

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:03.280
underneath the water?

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:08.690
To truly answer this question - if any answer
is possible at all - we need to go back to

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:14.210
the beginning, and ask ourselves a different
question: How does the SCP Foundation actually

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:17.470
find most of the anomalies it catalogs and
contains?

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:23.380
It’s a simple question with a multifaceted
answer, depending on the anomaly in question.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:28.170
For the most part, the Foundation has a network
of field agents embedded in pretty much every

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:32.850
institution across the globe, including rival
groups of interest like the Global Occult

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:34.980
Coalition and the Serpent’s Hand.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:40.690
If they so much as sniff the strange and unusual,
they alert the nearest site director and the

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:43.590
necessary personnel are dispatched to the
scene.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:48.070
There’s also the Foundation web crawlers,
which are a form of specialized software,

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:52.270
constantly patrolling the web for anomalous
activity that the Foundation wants to know

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:53.270
about.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:57.380
And one of the rarer, but still incredibly
important, methods of finding SCPs involve

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:00.070
looking into myths and local legends.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:05.020
Sure, that may seem like a good way to waste
time and resources, but the crossover between

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:08.860
recorded SCPs and folklore is surprisingly
common.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:14.230
Take SCP-1000, the formerly hyper-intelligent
apes that were nearly the dominant species

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:19.260
on earth until humans and a certain capricious
forest god pulled a dirty trick on them.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:24.380
They’re better known to most civilians as
the legendary Bigfoot or Sasquatch, perhaps

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.290
the most famous cryptid of all time.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:32.690
Or SCP-1337, the Hitchhiker, an anomalous
spectral entity that manifests in the cars

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:37.560
of those who don’t pick her up, and performs
horrific acts of violence against them.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:42.920
She’s eerily similar to legends you can
find not only all over the US but the entire

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:48.320
world, of ghostly hitchhikers intruding into
the cars of unwary travelers and scaring them

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:52.580
half to death - or worse, if you’re unlucky.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:57.960
Another case where myths and legends pointed
the SCP Foundation in exactly the right direction.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:04.010
And of course, there’s SCP-136, the terrifying
Naked Doll.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:08.290
This was an almost featureless children’s
doll found inside an abandoned house, but

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:12.820
prolonged time in its presence can make you
the victim of a warped apparition that’ll

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.520
drive you half-mad with fear.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.660
It’s got such a detrimental psychological
effect on people that the Foundation has been

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:23.569
controversially using it as a torture method
during “enhanced interrogation” sessions

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:26.520
with captured members of rival groups of interest.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.740
And how did they find it?

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:32.160
The Foundation keeps track of neighborhood
rumors about haunted houses with supposedly

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:33.989
supernatural inhabitants.

00:03:33.989 --> 00:03:38.959
Clearly, when it looks like it might actually
get results, no myth or local legend is too

00:03:38.959 --> 00:03:43.850
big or too small to warrant an investigation
from the SCP Foundation.

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:49.220
It was with this mindset that a younger, happier,
and less drunk Dr. B Reynard set off with

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:55.190
his team to Okanagan Lake, in search of what
locals had referred to as the legendary Ogopogo.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:04:00.099
We’ve all heard of the Loch Ness Monster,
the lake monster from Scotland that’s been

00:04:00.099 --> 00:04:04.239
turning heads for the better part of a century
- and may be related to two other similar

00:04:04.239 --> 00:04:12.680
SCPs, namely SCP-3934 and SCP-5533 - but the
Ogopogo is Canada’s answer to good ol’

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.680
Nessie.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.639
While the Loch Ness Monster resembles a plesiosaur,
the Ogopogo is much more serpentine, with

00:04:18.639 --> 00:04:22.049
a long, coiling body covered in green scales.

00:04:22.049 --> 00:04:25.939
Its long tail is said to be able to create
fierce storms along the surface of the water

00:04:25.939 --> 00:04:31.440
with its vicious whips, killing scores of
unfortunate adventurers who dared stray too

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:32.440
close.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:37.990
The name “Ogopogo” is also a palindrome,
meaning it reads the same forwards and backward,

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:41.960
and is believed to have originated in a novelty
song from the year 1924.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:47.370
However, it’s likely that the actual beast
this somewhat goofy name was given to is a

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:50.650
much older, fiercer, entity.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:55.520
And for the sake of his reputation as a researcher
as he took a plane to the Okanagan Valley,

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:59.360
Dr. Reynard very much hoped this was the case.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.729
Of course, he’d explored the legends heavily,
so much so that he was sure there had to be

00:05:03.729 --> 00:05:05.490
something to this whole thing.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:08.322
To the two tribes native to the area, the
Secwépemc and Syilx

00:05:08.322 --> 00:05:12.150
peoples, the lake-dwelling monster was known
as Naitaka, which has been loosely translated

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:17.220
into the “sacred creature of the water”,
the “water god”, and most menacingly of

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:18.900
all, the “water demon.”

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:23.830
The beast was often described in oral traditions
as being a malicious supernatural entity,

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:28.550
with great power and ill-intent towards those
trespassing on its territory.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:33.879
Legend has it that anyone who crosses Okanagan
Lake, the supposed domain of the Ogopogo,

00:05:33.879 --> 00:05:38.309
needs to make a sacrifice to the monster in
order to ensure safe passage.

00:05:38.309 --> 00:05:43.401
Those who refused to give the sacrifice the
beast demanded would pay a heavy toll: Being

00:05:43.401 --> 00:05:48.289
devoured or dragged down to a watery grave,
never to be seen again.

00:05:48.289 --> 00:05:51.479
And this monster isn’t just some old folktale,
either.

00:05:51.479 --> 00:05:56.479
Contemporary sightings have dated back to
1873, with both settlers and first nations

00:05:56.479 --> 00:06:00.409
people alike spotting the sinister Ogopogo
in the intervening years.

00:06:00.409 --> 00:06:04.529
Dr. Reynard had pored through the files on
hundreds of sightings - There were a number

00:06:04.529 --> 00:06:09.740
of incidents in the 1980s, so much so that
environmentalist group Greenpeace moved to

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:12.369
have the creature classified as a protected
species.

00:06:12.369 --> 00:06:16.930
Naturally, official sources decided against
the idea, claiming that none of the sightings

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:18.789
were of substance.

00:06:18.789 --> 00:06:24.349
In 1992, a vast shape filmed under the murky
water in Okanagan Lake was suggested to be

00:06:24.349 --> 00:06:26.249
the legendary beast.

00:06:26.249 --> 00:06:31.669
However, the FBI stepped in to deny the validity
of this case, stating that the beast was much

00:06:31.669 --> 00:06:36.509
more likely to be debris fallen off a local
tree, disappointing lovers of the strange

00:06:36.509 --> 00:06:38.219
and unusual everywhere.

00:06:38.219 --> 00:06:43.639
In 2011, nearly 20 years later, there was
more video footage of a sighting, showing

00:06:43.639 --> 00:06:47.520
large, dark shapes moving underneath the surface
of the Okanagan Lake.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:52.129
However, this claim was once again dismissed
by all outside parties, claiming the shape

00:06:52.129 --> 00:06:56.310
of the beast underneath the water was more
likely to be a pair of logs.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.310
Bummer.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:01.849
2018 was an exciting year for the Ogopogo,
with three different sightings of the creature

00:07:01.849 --> 00:07:05.089
being reported at different times throughout
the year.

00:07:05.089 --> 00:07:09.349
Witnesses described the creature as being
a giant snake, around fifty feet long, which

00:07:09.349 --> 00:07:13.559
is consistent with a lot of the historical
descriptions of the beast as well as being

00:07:13.559 --> 00:07:19.110
over twice as long as the reticulated python,
the non-anomalous longest snake in the world.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:23.679
So, naturally, authority figures once again
shot down the validity of any claims that

00:07:23.679 --> 00:07:26.399
the creature was actually real and out there.

00:07:26.399 --> 00:07:31.869
Dr. Reynard found it almost funny: They didn’t
even need to suppress knowledge of this creature.

00:07:31.869 --> 00:07:36.349
If it really was out there, mainstream sources
seemed to be doing their job for them and

00:07:36.349 --> 00:07:38.149
keeping the creature covered up.

00:07:38.149 --> 00:07:42.819
He was determined, though, that he would be
the one to prove to his superiors that this

00:07:42.819 --> 00:07:47.319
creature was indeed real, and lurking in Okanagan
Lake.

00:07:47.319 --> 00:07:51.949
He organized a number of varied investigative
missions: From actively trawling the lake

00:07:51.949 --> 00:07:56.330
itself, to conducting interviews with first-hand
witnesses as well as those who claimed to

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:59.229
see no merit in their evidence and testimony.

00:07:59.229 --> 00:08:03.839
Dr. Reynard noticed a strange phenomenon:
The people who’d seen it first-hand were

00:08:03.839 --> 00:08:08.199
as certain that it was real as the doubters
were that it was fake.

00:08:08.199 --> 00:08:12.390
Even for typical skeptics, the non-believers
seemed shockingly resolute that there really

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:18.099
was nothing down there, and the alleged photos
and videos were 100% bogus.

00:08:18.099 --> 00:08:22.959
Early diagnostic tests into the lake, directly
overseen by Dr. Reynard, seemed to point to

00:08:22.959 --> 00:08:25.319
a creature clearly being down there.

00:08:25.319 --> 00:08:29.520
He found the direct testimony both compelling
and consistent with what he and his team were

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:34.430
catching glimpses of, so why were people so
adamant that nothing was down there?

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:39.750
It was almost like the Ogopogo really was
as mystical as the First Nations legends said,

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:43.410
and it was casting a spell on all the non-believers.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:47.690
That was when it hit Dr. Reynard like a perfect
bolt of lightning: They weren’t just looking

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:52.930
at a particularly large sea snake with unnatural
longevity here, they were looking at a sea

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:56.050
serpent with cognitohazardous powers.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:09:00.580
It was a beast with a perfect defense mechanism
- Only those who saw it up close would actually

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:05.050
believe that the creature was real, anyone
who found out about it via secondary sources

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:08.330
would experience an extreme state of incredulity.

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:13.441
Nobody except those who saw it directly would
ever believe that it existed, and thus, even

00:09:13.441 --> 00:09:17.730
the most intelligent prey would lower their
defenses around its domain.

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:20.130
An elegant and dangerous anomalous hunter.

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:24.620
Dr. Reynard had found himself a worthy opponent,
and one that would help him make his mark

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:25.880
at the Foundation.

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:32.540
He drew up the file and gave it the designation
SCP-1933, before sending it back to his supervisors.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:36.870
They wrote back, saying they didn’t feel
as though there was enough of a basis in evidence

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:39.500
to deem this entry worthy of inclusion.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:44.450
If Dr. Reynard wanted to have his so-called
Ogopogo dignified with entry into the SCP

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:48.030
Foundation Archives, he needed to back it
up properly.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:53.360
This presented a problem to Dr. Reynard: How
could he provide documentation and evidence

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:58.110
for a creature that had the defining anomalous
power of making all of its own documentation

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.200
and evidence seem phony?

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:06.240
He was caught between a rock and a hard place,
with only one solution: Create the most undeniably

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:10.630
high-quality evidence of the creature that
the world had ever seen.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:14.780
Not long after that, his superiors at the
SCP Foundation would receive a video file

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.250
from Dr. Reynard.

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:20.440
According to the notes on his report, he’d
set up a trap using an elk carcass to lure

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:24.640
the creature out of the water, and capture
HD video of it feeding.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:29.450
When the senior researchers gathered around
to watch the video, they were astounded.

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:30.770
It was...An animatronic.

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:36.300
A cheap, rubber suit around a somewhat janky
robot, like something you’d see at a theme

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:37.300
park.

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:39.740
How much had Dr. Reynard spent on this absurd
farce?

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.110
Did he think this was funny?

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:47.000
Despite Dr. Reynard’s protests, he was reprimanded
severely for this waste of Foundation resources.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:52.910
The object class on his 1933 file was switched
to “EXPLAINED” - meaning a rational, non-anomalous

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:58.550
explanation for the observed phenomena had
been found, discrediting it - and the 1933

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:03.170
slot was instead filled with a strange, fat
man dressed as Santa Claus, whose bodily fluids

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:05.060
are all Irish Cream.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.670
The ultimate humiliation.

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:12.340
Dr. Reynard was left with nothing, and we
join him once again where we started, with

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:17.620
a drunken Dr. Reynard standing on the edge
of Okanagan Lake, staring hatefully into the

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:21.010
water as something seemed to move underneath.

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:25.840
If Dr. Reynard screamed that night, there
was nobody there to hear it.

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:28.530
His remains were dredged out of the lake the
next day.

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:33.010
His official cause of death was listed as
drowning after an unfortunate boating accident,

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:35.880
though the boat in question was never found.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:40.830
Reports that his corpse was found “half-eaten”
have mostly been dismissed as rumors.

00:11:40.830 --> 00:11:45.090
After all, there’s no such thing as the
Ogopogo.

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:50.090
Now go check out “SCP-1861 - The Crew of
the HMS Wintersheimer” and “The Horror

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:55.390
of Body Stealing Rain - SCP-3300” for more
ominous aquatic anomalies!

